# defaults_named.tkr — §9 C parameter defaults + `:=` named arguments, exercised end to end
# (default-fill, `:=` naming any parameter, positional-before-named, started-named -> all-named with
# free reordering, `:=` through a method dot-call, and `params` combined with a default) through one
# witness number.
#
# The witness reads back which binding ran, in arithmetic only the correct resolution produces:
#   defaults:      box(5)=523, box(5,7)=573, box(5,7,9)=579
#   name a param:  box(5, d := 9)=529, box(5, h := 4)=543, box(w := 6)=623
#   all named:     box(w := 5, d := 9, h := 4)=549
#   method `:=`:   B().vol()=21, B().vol(k := 5)=35
#   params+default: g(7)=7200, g(7,3)=7300, g(7,3,1,2)=7303, g(7, b := 4)=7400
# Sum = 33178. A relapse in any path moves the total off 33178.

Feature: defaults_named — a call fills defaults and binds `:=` named arguments, including through methods and `params`

  Scenario: every default-fill, `:=` naming, reordering, method, and params+default path binds correctly
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "33178"
